<title>USA: N.Y. boosts semiconductor research to create jobs.</title>
<headline>N.Y. boosts semiconductor research to create jobs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State University of New York in Albany is starting a pilot program in semiconductor research at its Center for Advanced Thin Film Technology.</p>
<p>The $4.5 million program, which is sponsored by the Semiconductor Industry Association, aims to help the Center create high-tech jobs in the area by encouraging entrepreneurs.</p>
<p>The program will study ways of using copper instead of aluminum interconnections on semiconducters.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
